  "description": "UXIGUG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H58 Dy1 N8 O36 Si8 Y3 2-,2(C8 H20 N1 1+),4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Dy1? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.688-3.701 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.06-107.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (Et4N)2[(PhSiO1.5)8(Y0.75Dy0.25O1.5)4(O)(NO2.5)6(EtOH)2(MeCN)2].",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
